<title>NEW ZEALAND: Air NZ half-yr profit down 43 pct.</title>
<headline>Air NZ half-yr profit down 43 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half yr to Dec 31.</p>
<p>			   (million NZ$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit				 76.74 vs 135.1</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)			   32.7 vs 60.9</p>
<p>    Div (cents)			    8.0 vs 8.0</p>
<p>    Turnover (billion)		  1.46 vs 1.50</p>
<p>    Pretax profit			 64.6 vs 155.2</p>
<p>    Tax credit			     0.6 vs 18.9 debit</p>
<p>    Equity earnings		     11.5 vs 1.5 loss</p>
<p>    Shares outstanding (million)   566.8 vs 443.5</p>
<p>Dividend carries full imputation credits.</p>
<p>Pay date April 1</p>
<p>Reg date March 21</p>
<p>Note - Air New Zealand Ltd is a New Zealand airline operator. Brierley Investments Ltd owns 42 percent of Air NZ.  </p>
<p>Balance sheet (in billions unless stated)</p>
<p>    Current assets			    0.85 vs 1.24</p>
<p>    Total assets				3.33 vs 3.27</p>
<p>    Current liabilities		     0.95 vs 1.01</p>
<p>    Total liabilities			 1.68 vs 1.87</p>
<p>    Shareholders' equity		    1.65 vs 1.40</p>
<p>Cashflow from operating activities  0.20 vs 0.27</p>
<p>Cashflow from investing activities(0.67) vs (0.09)</p>
